      '4. Choose cases deliberately: the happy path, boundaries (0, 1, many, max, empty, null), invalid input, error and failure paths, time and ordering, and the regression that prompted the test. Equivalence classes beat piles of near-identical cases; table-driven tests keep them compact. For pure functions, consider property-style checks (round trips, invariants, idempotence).',
