      '4. Front-end: avoid layout thrash and unnecessary renders (memoise expensive computations, stable keys, virtualise long lists), debounce input handlers, lazy-load routes and images, keep the main thread free (move heavy work to workers), ship less JavaScript, and measure with the browser profiler and Web Vitals.',
      '5. Memory: avoid unbounded caches and growing collections, release listeners and timers, prefer streaming to loading entire files, and be aware of copies (slicing, spreading, serialising).',
